      "references": "- https://github.com/expressjs/multer/security/advisories/GHSA-q7qp-rjg7-q26m\n- https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-113872\n- https://github.com/expressjs/multer/commit/80a2d9df1dfd63b5fab631b8b9966164ed647adf\n- https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html\n- https://github.com/expressjs/multer/releases/tag/v2.5.0\n- https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-q7qp-rjg7-q26m",
      "created": "2026-10-23T22:08:22.000Z",
      "id": 1243083,
      "npm_advisory_id": null,
      "overview": "### Impact\n\nWhen `multer` is configured with an asynchronous `fileFilter`, a single request can crash the Node.js process. If a request is aborted (for example when one file is rejected) while another file's async `fileFilter` is still pending, the pending callback later resumes a parsing stream that multer has already torn down. busboy then emits an error on a stream that no longer has an error listener, which Node raises as an unhandled `'error'` event, and the process exits. A single unauthenticated request is enough, so any application using `multer` with an asynchronous `fileFilter` is affected, regardless of storage engine. Uploads using a synchronous `fileFilter` are not affected.\n\n### Patches\n\nUsers should upgrade to `multer` `2.5.0` or later.\n\n### Workarounds\n\nUse a synchronous `fileFilter`.",
      "reported_by": null,
      "title": "multer vulnerable to Denial of Service via a pending asynchronous fileFilter after request teardown",
      "metadata": null,
      "cves": [
        "CVE-2026-113872"
      ],
